## 1. Executive Summary & Problem Framing
Modern Security Operations Centers (SOCs) face critical operational friction due to legacy rule-based Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) generating alert fatigue with false positive rates exceeding **90%**. Group 16 formulates network intrusion detection as a **5-class machine learning classification problem** using the authentic **NSL-KDD benchmark dataset** (41 predictive features).

### Threat Taxonomy
1. **Normal Traffic**
2. **Denial of Service (DoS)**
3. **Surveillance / Probing**
4. **Remote-to-Local (R2L)**
5. **User-to-Root (U2R)**

